Package: soilcnn
Title: Convolutional Neural Networks for Digital Soil Mapping
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Cássio", "Marques"), "Moquedace", , "cassiomoquedace@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(c("Clara", "Glória", "Oliveira"), "Baldi", role = "aut"))
Description: A framework, built on 'torch', for mapping a soil property from
    point observations and a stack of aligned rasters with a convolutional
    network that reads each point's neighbourhood. It extracts the patches,
    resamples by spatial blocks or by k-fold nearest neighbour distance
    matching, tunes and selects under a noise floor and the one-standard-error
    rule, refits the selected configuration under several seeds, and predicts
    median, mean and interval maps over rasters of any extent, with the area
    of applicability beside them. Random forest and multilayer perceptron
    baselines run under the same folds.
